{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.AdjoinRoot","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_ne_top_of_fourth_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_ne_top_of_fourth_root","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L178-L195","doc":"**A fourth root of unity keeps it.** If `q² = −1` (so `[2]_q = 0`) and `2 ≠ 0` in `K`, the\nKähler ideal of `H₂(q)` is proper: `HH_1(H₂(q)/K) ≠ 0`. This is the `n = 2` shadow of the\nnon-semisimple root-of-unity fibre, and — read through `ℤ[q^{±1}] → K`, `q ↦ i` — of the\nnon-formality of the tower ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_eq_top_of_qint_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_eq_top_of_qint_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L170-L176","doc":"**Generic `q` kills the degree.** If `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹ ≠ 0` (every generic `q`, and the\nsubstrate `q₀`), the Kähler ideal of `H₂(q)` is everything: `HH_1(H₂(q)/K) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.two_x_sub_h_sq_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.two_x_sub_h_sq_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L163-L168","doc":"The discriminant identity in the corpus's own `H₂(q)`: `(2σ₁ − h)² = [2]_q²`. The two-strand\nHecke algebra of `QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2` is `Aq (heckeParam K q)` definitionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.heckeParam_sq_add_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.heckeParam_sq_add_four","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L155-L161","doc":"At the Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹` (`q ≠ 0`), the discriminant is the square of the quantum\ninteger: `h² + 4 = (q + q⁻¹)² = [2]_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_ne_top_of_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_ne_top_of_hom","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L119-L147","doc":"**The tower has one.** If a ring homomorphism `φ : R →+* K` into a field with `2 ≠ 0` sends\n`h² + 4` to `0`, then `(2x − h) ≠ A_h`, so `A_h/(2x − h) ≠ 0`: `Ω¹ = HH_1 ≠ 0` (cited\nidentification). The witness is the evaluation `x ↦ φ(h)/2`, under which the quadratic becomes\n`(X − φ(h)/2)²` and `2x − h ↦ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_eq_top_of_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal_eq_top_of_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L107-L117","doc":"**The fibre has no degree.** If `h² + 4` is a unit of `R`, the ideal `(2x − h)` is the whole\nof `A_h`, so `A_h/(2x − h) = 0`: `Ω¹ = HH_1 = 0` (cited identification). At `h = q − q⁻¹`, `h² + 4\n= [2]_q²`, invertible at every generic `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.two_x_sub_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.two_x_sub_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L99-L105","doc":"**The discriminant identity.** `(2x − h)² = h² + 4` in `A_h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.x_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.x_sq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L91-L97","doc":"The Hecke quadratic relation in `A_h`: `x² = h·x + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerIdeal","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The ideal `(2x − h) ⊆ A_h`; `A_h / (2x − h) ≅ Ω¹_{A_h/R} ≅ HH_1(A_h/R)` (cited, see header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.kaehlerGen","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The element `f'(x) = 2x − h` whose principal ideal presents `Ω¹_{A_h/R}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.x","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L82-L83","doc":"The generator `x = σ₁`, the image of `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.Aq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.Aq","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L79-L80","doc":"`A_h := R[X]/(X² − h X − 1)` — the two-strand Hecke algebra with parameter `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.quadPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2KaehlerDegrees.quadPoly","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2KaehlerDegrees.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The Hecke quadratic `X² − h·X − 1` with an arbitrary parameter `h`. At `h = q − q⁻¹` this is\n`QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2.heckePoly` syntactically. ","signatureChunk":0}]}